--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI EfficiencyPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable EfficiencyDataSource seam whose methods keep
the web hook names at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles,
useDrivingStats ← GET /drives/stats, useDrives ← GET /drives?vehicle_id). The web per-drive efficiency
heuristic (getEfficiency: (battUsed * 0.75 * 1000) / (distanceM / 1000) Wh/km) and every chart/table
aggregation (dailyTrend, speedVsEff, tempVsEff, speedDist, tempBuckets — the web useMemo blocks) are
ported verbatim into the deterministic, harness-verified EfficiencyEngine. Unit conversion is injected
into the engine as closures so the bucketing/aggregation is pure + testable; the production view builds
those closures from the shared KMP Units facade (P1/S5) at the render boundary only (ADR-005). The
DrivingStats wire fields carry legacy unit suffixes (avgSpeedKmh, totalDistanceKm, …) but hold SI base
values — the web feeds them straight into convertSpeedFromSI / convertDistanceFromSI (which expect m/s
and meters) — so the model stores them SI and records the SI base unit on disk.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
RangePicker date filter) and ALL of the web's sections, each with its own empty/loading/error states:

  Hero gauges (GlassPanel1 + RadialGauge avg-consumption tinted by efficiency tier, + km/kWh + CO₂ +
  total distance), the four summary stat cards (GlassPanel2/3/4/5 Avg-Consumption / Avg-Speed /
  Est-Cost-per-km / Drives-Analyzed) with the noStatCards empty (GlassPanel6), the daily-efficiency
  area chart (efficiency-dailyTrend ChartContainer + AreaChart), the efficiency-by-speed-range bar
  chart (Efficiency-by-Speed-Range ChartContainer + BarChart), the speed-vs-efficiency and
  temperature-vs-efficiency scatter plots (ChartContainer + ScatterChart), the temperature-bucketed
  table (GlassPanel11 + DataTable), the metric-bar summary (GlassPanel12), and the energy insights
  (GlassPanel13). The four chart panels always render (never hidden) — each shows its data above the
  web threshold (dailyTrend>2, speedVsEff>3, tempVsEff>3) else its own not-enough-data overlay.

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the hero grid, the stat-card grid, the two chart rows, the summary grid, and
the insights grid reflow for macOS / iPad regular width vs. compact iPhone. The page is registered for
the new `.efficiency` AppRoute (web /efficiency resolves to it directly via the canonical path
segment; grouped under .vehicle alongside .driving) and hosted through EfficiencyRouteRegistration in
TeslaSyncApp. All 42 visible strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; SI
units render via Units + EfficiencyPageFormat at the boundary.

  NOTE — name reconciliation: the page formatter is `EfficiencyPageFormat` (not `EfficiencyFormat`):
  the feature-views EfficiencyPanel.Adapter already declares a public `EfficiencyFormat` in the same
  module, so the page formatter is uniquely named to avoid the redeclaration. All other Efficiency*
  type names are module-unique.

